WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:02.670
BUKOLA AYODELE: Today, we're
talking about security gaming

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.830
advancements in a new region.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.980
I'm Bukola, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.410
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.470
Cloud Armor and Google
Cloud's DDoS defense service

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.360
and Web Application Firewall--

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.440
WAF-- help customers protect
their websites and services.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.290
We work constantly to stay
ahead of the evolving threat

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.390
landscape and are
excited to announce

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.650
a few updates, including the
preview of Cloud Armor Adaptive

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.500
Protection, a machine
learning-powered capability

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.340
to protect your applications
and services from layer 7 DDoS

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.990
attacks, four new preconfigured
WAF rules, and a reference

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.130
architecture.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.220
Check out the blog
for more details.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.950
Developed in collaboration
with Embark Studios,

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.220
Quilkin is a UDP
proxy tailor-made

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.640
for high-performance,
real-time multiplayer games.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.300
With Quilkin, our aim is to
pull common functionality

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.370
and provide this
common functionality

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.430
in a composable and
configurable way, leading

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.459
to a reusable foundation that
allows game developers to spend

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:08.430
more time on building
the game-specific aspects

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.190
of building their multiplayer
communication protocols,

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.130
rather than the common aspects.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.460
To support customers and public
sector in India and across

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.910
Asia-Pacific, we're excited to
announce that our new Google

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.240
Cloud region in Delhi
National Capital Region--

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.550
NCR-- is now open.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:30.300
Designed to help both Indian
and global companies alike build

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.250
highly-available applications
for their customers,

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.450
the Delhi NCR region is
our second Google Cloud

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.587
region in India and our tenth
to open in Asia-Pacific.

00:01:41.587 --> 00:01:43.670
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.350
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.320
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.760
We'll see you in the Cloud.

